## Snapshot tests

PRs that change visible Ecosia UI (`Ecosia/UI/**` or `Client/Ecosia/UI/**`) must also update snapshot tests and `SnapshotArtifacts` references. See the [snapshot coverage map](firefox-ios/Ecosia/Ecosia.docc/SNAPSHOT_TESTING_WIKI.md#snapshot-coverage-map).

**If this PR has no visual UI impact** (e.g. refactor, logic-only, accessibility identifiers), you must add the **`skip-snapshot-check`** label **before opening the PR**. CI runs the snapshot update check as soon as the PR is created; adding the label afterward still works, but you may see a failed check until you add it and re-run the workflow.

## Before merging

### Checklist

- [ ] I performed some relevant testing on a real device and/or simulator for both iPhone and iPad
- [ ] I wrote Unit Tests that confirm the expected behaviour
- [ ] If this PR changes visible Ecosia UI (`Ecosia/UI/**` or `Client/Ecosia/UI/**`), I updated or added snapshot tests and `SnapshotArtifacts` references — **or** I added the `skip-snapshot-check` label **before opening the PR** because there is no visual impact (see [Snapshot tests](#snapshot-tests) above)
- [ ] I updated only the [english localization source files](Client/Ecosia/L10N/es.lproj) if needed
- [ ] I added the `// Ecosia:` helper comments where needed
- [ ] I made sure that any change to the Analytics events included in PR won't alter current analytics (e.g. new users, upgrading users)
- [ ] I included documentation updates to the coding standards or Confluence doc, when needed